<article class="env-lemma" id="01MZ">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/01MZ">Lemma <span data-tag="01MZ">27.11.2</span>.</a> Let $A$, $B$, and $C$ be graded rings. Set $X = \text{Proj}(A)$, $Y = \text{Proj}(B)$ and $Z = \text{Proj}(C)$. Let $\varphi : A \to B$, $\psi : B \to C$ be graded ring maps. Then we have </p>
  <div class="equation">
  \[  U(\psi \circ \varphi ) = r_\psi ^{-1}(U(\varphi )) \quad \text{and} \quad r_{\psi \circ \varphi } = r_\varphi \circ r_\psi |_{U(\psi \circ \varphi )}.  \]
</div>
  <p> In addition we have </p>
  <div class="equation">
  \[  \theta _\psi \circ r_\psi ^*\theta _\varphi = \theta _{\psi \circ \varphi }  \]
</div>
  <p> with obvious notation. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      Omitted. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>